    "description": "Read source: a whole file by path, a line window (start_line/end_line, no size cap unless max_lines is set), a declaration by name (symbol_locator; Go and Python resolve natively, other languages through the language server), or several of those at once with targets. Responses carry the content, the document revision and the line count; a multi-target reply lists every target's size under entries before the bodies. max_lines caps a delivery and the reply says truncated with the total, so read a big file with max_lines or view=outline first, then window what matters.",
